  steps:
  - requiredAction: 1
    targetLabel: Lab coat
    title: Welcome to IGH Genomics
    instruction: Point at and select the lab coat.
    explanation: The lab coat is part of personal protective equipment.
    narrationKey: TourLabCoat
  - requiredAction: 2
    targetLabel: Blue nitrile gloves
    title: Protect your hands
    instruction: Select the blue nitrile gloves.
    explanation: Clean gloves reduce contamination and protect the learner.
    narrationKey: TourGloves
  - requiredAction: 3
    targetLabel: Handwashing sink
    title: Handwashing area
    instruction: Select the laboratory sink.
    explanation: Hand hygiene comes before and after laboratory work.
    narrationKey: TourSink
  - requiredAction: 4
    targetLabel: Prepared qPCR plate
    title: Team 4 handoff
    instruction: Select the prepared qPCR plate.
    explanation: Team 5 receives a filled, mapped and sealed plate; it does not remix
      the reactions.
    narrationKey: TourPreparedPlate
  - requiredAction: 5
    targetLabel: Optical seal
    title: Optical seal
    instruction: Select the transparent seal on top of the plate.
    explanation: The instrument reads fluorescence through this seal.
    narrationKey: TourOpticalSeal
  - requiredAction: 6
    targetLabel: Real-time PCR machine
    title: qPCR instrument
    instruction: Select the real-time PCR machine.
    explanation: It changes temperature and measures fluorescence during the run.
    narrationKey: TourInstrument
  - requiredAction: 7
    targetLabel: Instrument touchscreen
    title: Instrument touchscreen
    instruction: Select the touchscreen.
    explanation: This is where the protocol is checked before loading.
    narrationKey: TourTouchscreen
  - requiredAction: 8
    targetLabel: Motorized drawer
    title: Motorized drawer
    instruction: Select the plate drawer.
    explanation: The drawer carries the plate into the instrument.
    narrationKey: TourDrawer
  - requiredAction: 9
    targetLabel: Thermal block
    title: Thermal block
    instruction: Select the thermal block inside the drawer.
    explanation: The block performs denaturation, annealing and extension temperatures.
    narrationKey: TourThermalBlock
  - requiredAction: 10
    targetLabel: Results monitor
    title: Results monitor
    instruction: Select the monitor.
    explanation: Amplification curves and control results appear here.
    narrationKey: TourMonitor
  - requiredAction: 11
    targetLabel: Plate centrifuge
    title: Plate centrifuge
    instruction: Select the plate centrifuge.
    explanation: It is background equipment in Team 5, but explains how liquid is
      collected before handoff.
    narrationKey: TourCentrifuge
  - requiredAction: 12
    targetLabel: Biohazard waste container
    title: Waste containers
    instruction: Select the biohazard waste container to finish the lab tour.
    explanation: Correct waste separation is part of safe laboratory work.
    narrationKey: TourWaste
  - requiredAction: 13
    targetLabel: Power button
    title: Power on
    instruction: Physically press the green Power button on the machine.
    explanation: The instrument must be powered before its controls unlock.
    narrationKey: PowerOnInstrument
  - requiredAction: 14
    targetLabel: Validate protocol button
    title: Configure the qPCR run
    instruction: Review the touchscreen values, correct any red field, then press
      Validate protocol.
    explanation: This teaching programme uses 35 cycles and fluorescence acquisition
      at 60 degrees Celsius.
    narrationKey: ValidateProtocol
  - requiredAction: 15
    targetLabel: Plate ID
    title: Check the plate ID
    instruction: Select the plate ID label.
    explanation: The ID confirms the plate belongs to this run.
    narrationKey: InspectPlateId
  - requiredAction: 16
    targetLabel: Optical seal checkpoint
    title: Inspect the seal
    instruction: Select the optical seal checkpoint.
    explanation: The seal must be intact and firmly attached.
    narrationKey: InspectOpticalSeal
  - requiredAction: 17
    targetLabel: Bubble-check area
    title: Inspect for bubbles
    instruction: Select the bubble-check area.
    explanation: Large bubbles can disturb the fluorescence reading.
    narrationKey: InspectBubbles
  - requiredAction: 18
    targetLabel: A1 marker
    title: Find A1
    instruction: Select the A1 marker at the reference corner.
    explanation: A1 tells you which way the plate must face.
    narrationKey: InspectA1Marker
  - requiredAction: 19
    targetLabel: Drawer-open button
    title: Open the drawer
    instruction: Press the blue drawer-open button.
    explanation: The motorized drawer exposes the loading socket.
    narrationKey: OpenDrawer
  - requiredAction: 20
    targetLabel: Prepared qPCR plate
    title: Load the plate
    instruction: Pinch or grip the plate, align A1, and place it in the socket.
    explanation: Wrongly rotated plates are rejected and cannot snap into place.
    narrationKey: SeatPlate
  - requiredAction: 21
    targetLabel: Drawer-close button
    title: Close the drawer
    instruction: Press the amber drawer-close button.
    explanation: The drawer only closes after the plate is correctly seated.
    narrationKey: CloseDrawer
  - requiredAction: 22
    targetLabel: Start button
    title: Start amplification
    instruction: Press the green Start button.
    explanation: Final scientific validation runs before the 35-cycle simulation
      begins.
    narrationKey: StartRun
  - requiredAction: 25
    targetLabel: Amplification display
    title: Observe 35 cycles
    instruction: Watch the temperature, cycle counter and amplification curves build.
    explanation: The educational run is compressed to about 30 seconds.
    narrationKey: ObserveAmplification
  - requiredAction: 23
    targetLabel: Control interpretation
    title: Interpret the controls
    instruction: Choose the statement that correctly describes the positive control
      and NTC.
    explanation: The positive control must amplify. The no-template control must
      stay flat.
    narrationKey: InterpretControlsPassed
